<title>USA: Bio-Plexus Inc Q1 loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Bio-Plexus Inc Q1 loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>TOLLAND, Conn. 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997		  1996</p>
<p>Revenue</p>
<p>   Sales			     $  1,112,000	  $  453,000</p>
<p>   Licensing Fees		     1,500,000		    --</p>
<p>     Total Revenue		    2,612,000	     453,000</p>
<p>Costs and expenses:</p>
<p>   Research and development	   425,000	     380,000</p>
<p>Other operating and</p>
<p>    engineering costs		 1,610,000	     942,000</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>    administrative		    1,876,000	   1,594,000</p>
<p>Total operating costs</p>
<p>	and expenses		    3,911,000	   2,916,000</p>
<p>Financing expenses:</p>
<p>CII debt:</p>
<p>   Interest expense			 1,000		 6,000</p>
<p>Amortization of deferred</p>
<p>    debt financing			 33,000		29,000</p>
<p> Other financing expenses	   1,074,000	     276,000</p>
<p>   Total financing expenses	 1,108,000	     311,000</p>
<p> Net loss			     (2,407,000)	 (2,774,000)</p>
<p> Net loss per common share	     (0.33)		(0.42)</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>   outstanding			  7,371,577	   6,576,783</p>
<p>NOTE: Company said Q1 1997 includes one-time charge of $640,000 for reduction in long-term debt; the charge includes $490,000 for a reduction in warrants and $150,000 in interest paid.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
